Changes code from Helium's helium/core/web-push-service.patch (GPL-3.0, The Helium Authors).

Helium 0.22 adds web push through its own autopush server: a WebSocket kept open to push.helium.computer for sites
with a push subscription, behind the HeliumWebPush feature (off by default) and Helium's services consent. Ray
never turns Helium's services on, so it stays off for good here: ShouldAccessPushService is false whatever the prefs
say, the default push server is the unresolvable services placeholder, and the GCM profile service never builds the
autopush driver, whatever the feature says. The driver's code stays and compiles.

--- a/components/helium_services/helium_services_helpers.cc
+++ b/components/helium_services/helium_services_helpers.cc
@@ -113,8 +113,7 @@
 }
 
 bool ShouldAccessPushService(const PrefService& prefs) {
-  return ShouldAccessServices(prefs) &&
-         prefs.GetBoolean(prefs::kHeliumWebPushEnabled);
+  return false;
 }
 
 GURL GetExtensionUpdateURL(const PrefService& prefs) {
